ld tapped.\\nWhen Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{U}.", 'Spectacle {R} (You may cast this spell for its spectacle cost rather than its mana cost if an opponent lost life this turn.)\\nExile the top two cards of your library. Until the end of your next turn, you may play those cards.', 'Spit Flame deals 4 damage to target creature.\\nWhenever a Dragon enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {R}. If you do, return Spit Flame from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Target opponent chooses X cards from their hand. Look at those cards. You may cast a spell from among them without paying its mana cost.', "Target player sacrifices a creature. You gain life equal to that creature's toughness.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)", 'The first spell you cast from exile each turn has cascade. (When you cast your first spell from exile, exile cards from the top of your library until you exile a nonland card that costs less. You may cast it without paying its mana cost. Put the exiled cards on the bottom of your library in a random order.)', 'The next spell you cast this turn can be cast as though it had flash. When you next cast a spell this turn, put X +1/+1 counters on up to one target creature, where X is the mana value of that spell.', "The owner of target permanent shuffles it into their library, then reveals the top card of their library. If it's a permanent card, they put it onto the battlefield.", 'Thriving Grove enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Grove enters the battlefield, choose a color other than green.\\n{T}: Add {G} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Thriving Heath enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Heath enters the battlefield, choose a color other than white.\\n{T}: Add {W} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Thriving Isle enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Isle enters the battlefield, choose a color other than blue.\\n{T}: Add {U} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Thriving Moor enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Moor enters the battlefield, choose a color other than black.\\n{T}: Add {B} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Trample\\nWhenever a source you control deals 5 or more damage to a player, draw a card.', 'Until end of turn, permanents your opponents control gain "When this permanent deals damage to the player who cast Hellish Rebuke, sacrifice this permanent. You lose 2 life."', 'Vigilance', 'Vigilance\\nWhen Cataclysmic Gearhulk enters the battlefield, each player chooses an artifact, a creature, an enchantment, and a planeswalker from among the nonland permanents they control, then sacrifices the rest.', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Sun Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may return target permanent card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Vigilance\\nYou may look at the top card of your library any time.\\nYou may cast Aura and Equipment spells from the top of your library. When you cast an Equipment spell this way, it gains "When this Equipment enters the battlefield, attach it to target creature you control."', 'Ward {3}\\nOther creatures you control have ward {3}.\\nWhenever Storvald enters the battlefield or attacks, choose one or both —\\n• Target creature has base power and toughness 7/7 until end of turn.\\n• Target creature has base power and toughness 1/1 until end of turn.', "When Champion of Wits enters the battlefield, you may draw cards equal to its power. If you do, discard two cards.\\nEternalize {5}{U}{U} ({5}{U}{U}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a 4/4 black Zombie Naga Wizard with no mana cost. Eternalize only as a sorcery.)", 'When Chittering Witch enters the battlefield, create a number of 1/1 black Rat creature tokens equal to the number of opponents you have.\\n{1}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', "When Druid of Purification enters the battlefield, starting with you, each player may choose an artifact or enchantment you don't control. Destroy each permanent chosen this way.", "When Garruk's Uprising enters the battlefield, if you control a creature with power 4 or greater, draw a card.\\nCreatures you control have trample. (They can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker they're attacking.)\\nWhenever a creature with power 4 or greater enters the battlefield under your control, draw a card.", 'When Hostage Taker enters the battlefield, exile another target creature or artifact until Hostage Taker leaves the battlefield. You may cast that card for as long as it remains exiled, and mana of any type can be spent to cast that spell.', 'When Knight of Autumn enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Put two +1/+1 counters on Knight of Autumn.\\n• Destroy target artifact or enchantment.\\n• You gain 4 life.', 'When Meteor Golem enters the battlefield, destroy target nonland permanent an opponent controls.', "When Nihiloor enters the battlefield, for each opponent, tap up to one untapped creature you control. When you do, gain control of target creature that player controls with power less than or equal to the tapped creature's power for as long as you control Nihiloor.\\nWhenever you attack with a creature an opponent owns, you gain 2 life and that player loses 2 life.", "When Plaguecrafter enters the battlefield, each player sacrifices a creature or planeswalker. Each player who can't discards a card.", 'When Riverwise Augur enters the battlefield, draw three cards, then put two cards from your hand on top of your library in any order.', "When Share the Spoils enters the battlefield or an opponent loses the game, exile the top card of each player's library.\\nDuring each player's turn, that player may play a land or cast a spell from among cards exiled with Share the Spoils, and they may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast that spell. When they do, exile the top card of their library.", 'When Solemn Simulacrum enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhen Solemn Simulacrum dies, you may draw a card.', 'When Zhalfirin Void enters the battlefield, scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)\\n{T}: Add {C}.', "Whenever Etali, Primal Storm attacks, exile the top card of each player's library, then you may cast any number of spells from among those cards without paying their mana costs.", 'Whenever Fey Steed attacks, another target attacking creature you control gains indestructible until end of turn.\\nWhenever a creature or planeswalker you control becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever Tectonic Giant attacks or becomes the target of a spell an opponent controls, choose one —\\n• Tectonic Giant deals 3 damage to each opponent.\\n• Exile the top two cards of your library. Choose one of them. Until the end of your next turn, you may play that card.', "Whenever a Dragon enters the battlefield under your control, put a gold counter on Dragon's Hoard.\\n{T}, Remove a gold counter from Dragon's Hoard: Draw a card.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.", 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, it deals damage equal to its power to any target.', 'Whenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell, exile it instead of putting it into a graveyard as it resolves.\\n{X}, {T}, Sacrifice Rod of Absorption: You may cast any number of spells from among cards exiled with Rod of Absorption with total mana value X or less without paying their mana costs.', 'Whenever an Equipment enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card.\\nMetalcraft — Equipment you control have equip {0} as long as you control three or more artifacts.', 'Whenever another nontoken creature dies, you may create a 1/1 black Rat creature token.\\nRats you control have deathtouch.', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks or blocks, it and Zombies you control gain deathtouch until end of turn.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, create that many 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens.\\nEquip {3}', "Whenever equipped creature attacks, look at the top card of your library. If it's a land card, you may put it onto the battlefield tapped.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on it.\\nWhenever equipped creature deals combat damage, roll a d12. If the result is greater than the damage dealt or the result is 12, double the number of +1/+1 counters on that creature.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever one or more creature cards are put into your graveyard from anywhere, venture into the dungeon. This ability triggers only once each turn. (To venture into the dungeon, enter the first room or advance to the next room.)\\nCreate Undead — Whenever you complete a dungeon, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Whenever one or more creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, create two Treasure tokens.\\n{B}, Sacrifice X Treasures: Target creature gets -X/-X until end of turn. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Whenever you attack a player, tap target creature that player controls and goad it. (Until your next turn, that creature attacks each combat if able and attacks a player other than you if able.)\\nWhenever an opponent attacks another one of your opponents, you and the attacking player each draw a card and lose 1 life.', 'Whenever you attack, investigate. (Create a Clue token. It\'s an artifact with "{2}, Sacrifice this artifact: Draw a card.")\\nWhenever you sacrifice a Clue, venture into the dungeon. (Enter the first room or advance to the next room.)', 'Whenever you cast an Aura, Equipment, or Vehicle spell, draw a card.', 'Whenever you draw your second card each turn, create a 1/1 blue Illusion creature token with "This creature gets +1/+0 for each other Illusion you control."\\nWhenever an Illusion you control dies, you may put a permanent card with mana value less than or equal to that creature\'s power from your hand onto the battlefield.', "Whenever you sacrifice another nontoken artifact or creature, exile it.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice another artifact or creature: Draw a card.\\n{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Bag of Devouring: Roll a d10. Return up to X cards from among cards exiled with Bag of Devouring to their owners' hands, where X is the result.", "You may choose not to untap Immovable Rod during your untap step.\\nWhenever Immovable Rod becomes untapped, venture into the dungeon.\\n{3}{W}, {T}: For as long as Immovable Rod remains tapped, another target permanent loses all abilities and can't attack or block.", 'You may have Masterwork of Ingenuity enter the battlefield as a copy of any Equipment on the battlefield.', 'You may have Phantasmal Image enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield, except it\'s an Illusion in addition to its other types and it has "When this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it."', 'You may play an additional land this turn.\\nDraw a card.', '{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Exile the top card of your library. You may play that card this turn. (You still pay its costs. You can play a land this way only if you have an available land play remaining.)', '{1}, {T}: Add {B}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{W}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {R}{G}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{U}.', "{1}, {T}: Roll a d4 and create a number of Treasure tokens equal to the result. The player to your right gains control of Bucknard's Everfull Purse.", '{1}{B}: Return Reassembling Skeleton from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Wayfarer's Bauble: Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", '{3}, Sacrifice Burnished Hart: Search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{3}{G}{W}: Monstrosity 1. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put a +1/+1 counter on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nAs long as Fleecemane Lion is monstrous, it has hexproof and indestructible.", "{4}, {T}: Target opponent exiles cards from the top of their library until they exile an instant or sorcery card. You may cast that card without paying its mana cost. Then put the exiled cards that weren't cast this way on the bottom of that library in a random order.", '{4}{G}, {T}: Roll a d8. Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal a creature card with mana value equal to the result. Put that card onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', "{6}, Roll a d8: Monstrosity X, where X is the result. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put X +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nBerserk — When Clay Golem becomes monstrous, destroy target permanent.", '{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Doomed Necromancer: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{T}, Remove a component counter from Component Pouch: Add two mana of different colors.\\n{T}: Roll a d20.\\n1—9 | Put a component counter on Component Pouch.\\n10—20 | Put two component counters on Component Pouch.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.\\nSacrifice Commander's Sphere: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Bant Panorama: Search your library for a basic Forest, Plains, or Island card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Esper Panorama: Search your library for a basic Plains, Island, or Swamp card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Put a storage counter on Crucible of the Spirit Dragon.\\n{T}, Remove X storage counters from Crucible of the Spirit Dragon: Add X mana in any combination of colors. Spend this mana only to cast Dragon spells or activate abilities of Dragons.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Mishra's Factory becomes a 2/2 Assembly-Worker artifact creature until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{T}: Target Assembly-Worker creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Each player draws a card, then discards a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{G}{W}, {T}: Create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{5}, {T}, Exile Underdark Rift: Roll a d10. Put target artifact, creature, or planeswalker into its owner's library just beneath the top X cards of that library, where X is the result. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Unstable Obelisk: Destroy target permanent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast a Dragon creature spell.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Haven of the Spirit Dragon: Return target Dragon creature card or Ugin planeswalker card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Talisman of Indulgence deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W}. Activate only if you control an Island.\\n{T}: Add {U}. Activate only if you control a Plains.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Desert deals 1 damage to target attacking creature. Activate only during the end of combat step.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.\\n{2}{U}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Obsessive Stitcher: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.']
flavor: ['"Approach my tower on bended knee or depart from it as ash upon the wind."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"As I desire, so it shall be."\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"As this conflict grows, it gets harder to prevent the city from breaking down. How much longer can we keep this machinery balanced?"', '"Better the dead depart utterly than be enslaved."', '"Control the Great Conduit? You might as well try to divert a river with your hands."', '"Die. But die knowing that your pathetic life will yield a great bounty for me."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"Every choice alters the path of fate."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Her hunger knows no limit. Left unchecked, she would feast on all of Tarkir."\\n—Yasova Dragonclaw', '"His tenement is filled with the most vile, disgusting vermin. It\'s infested with rats, too."\\n—Branko One-Ear', '"I came seeking a challenge. All I found was you."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"I search for a vision of Zendikar that does not include the Eldrazi."\\n—Expedition journal entry', '"I was raised on stories of my ancestors, and I want to write my own pages in the tales."', '"If it has ears, it will dance to my tune."', '"It was a strange morning. When we awoke, we found our trees transformed. We didn\'t know whether to water them or polish them."\\n—Pulan, Bant orchardist', '"It\'s easy to get taken in by the spectacle, to enjoy a bit of naughty amusement. But make no mistake: the Cult of Rakdos is a danger."\\n—Tajic', '"Listen to the roar! Feel the thunder! The Immersturm shouts its approval with every bolt of lightning!"', '"Might doesn\'t just build empires. It protects them."\\n—Inti, Sun Empire knight', '"Molten earth has no anger of its own. Only by infusing it with your own rage can the magma seethe and take shape."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"Monsters dwell in every heart. We only think civilization tames them." ―Euphemia, Nexus watcher', '"My power is generosity, in a way. I give my survivors an appreciation for their lives."', '"Only victory shall stop our charge!"', '"Places, everyone!"\\n—Judith', '"Return to the earth and the wind."', '"Stay close, and their wrathful flames will not harm you."\\n—Galea', '"The cost of your opposition will be extracted from your wits."\\n—Nekusar, the Mindrazer', '"The crucible yields what you have forged in your mind. You need only reach in and draw the masterwork forth."\\n—Wahara, Keeper of the Crucible', '"The curse is broken."', '"The heavens augur weal . . . for me. Woe for you."', '"The wind whispers, \'come home,\' but I cannot."\\n—Teferi', '"Then we burn together!"', '"There are many kinds of duty, and mine is to see our world grow and endure."', '"There shall be a vast shout and then a vaster silence."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"There\'s only one way to be sure it\'s really dead."', '"There\'s wisdom to be gained in death—whether it be one\'s own or someone else\'s."\\n—Jarad, Golgari Lich-Lord', '"They may show up with the wrong thigh bone or mandible, but they always show up."\\n—Zul Ashur, lich lord', '"This world will be ruled by its rightful sovereigns, not these hideous pretenders."', '"Time flows as the rivers do, toward an unknown sea. The wise know to look downstream."', '"We must rely on our own knowledge, not on the dogma of the seekers or the mutterings of the sphinxes."\\n—Tullus of Palandius', '"We speak the dragons\' language of flame and rage. They speak our language of fury and honor. Together we shall weave a tale of destruction without equal."', '"We train for the improbable, like lightning striking the same place twice, or striking everywhere at once."\\n—Nundari, Sea Gate militia captain', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"What is mana but possibility, an idea not yet given form?"\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"Where will you run when I punish you with the very ground you flee on?"\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"Yes, nature is stronger. You don\'t see little buildings sprouting on trees."\\n—Emmara', '"Zendikar will triumph this day, and our armies will fly with angels."', 'A blazing sun that never sets.', "A dragon's scale can be carved into a mighty shield, provided you can procure a dragontooth to cut it.", 'A fiery scourge for both flesh and soul.', "A knight's devotion to their steed goes only so far.", 'After lightning struck the cliffs, the ore became iron, the iron became steel, and the steel became greaves. The lightning never left.', 'All are welcome.', 'All crave the Blessed Sleep. Few receive it.', 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', 'All suns must set.', "All the aether charts in the world can't compete with the trained eye of a talented scout.", 'All the wonders of the natural world in one breathtaking microcosm.', "An explorer's reward is a view of tomorrow's possibilities.", "As long as it's never left empty, this magic pouch produces coins every dawn.", 'Atarka conquered Qadat, the Fire Rim, long ago, winning over its efreet with a promise to spread the glory of fire to all the world.', 'Atarka serving-goblins coat themselves with grease imbued with noxious herbs, hoping to discourage their ravenous masters from adding them to the meal.', "Attracting a dragon's attention may be the last mistake you make.", 'Bant is a world where death and chaos hold no sway.', "Bant's hearts are as pure as its air and as bright as its skies.", 'Beauty appears in strange places for those with eyes to see it.', 'Beauty is in the eye of the exploder.', "Dinner and politics don't mix.", 'Divine light forged in steel.', "Druidcraft is a simple invocation to spirits of nature, promising a glimpse of nature's secrets.", 'Druids hold certain plants to be sacred and use their leaves and wood as a spellcasting focus.', 'During their endless travels, the mages of the Goma Fada caravan have learned ways to harness both life and death.', 'Each configuration reveals a potential future.', 'Esper is an expansive canvas painted by precise, controlling hands.', 'Even more than carrion, they crave the last words of the dying.', 'Eyes are unnecessary for seeing the future.', 'Far from human eyes, birds flit between vivid blossoms in a hidden paradise.', 'First, whispers of ancient days. Then, visions of things to come.', "For wisdom's sake, it was built high to gaze on all things. For glory's sake, it was built high as a testament of power. For strength's sake, it was built high to repel all attacks.", 'Forged by divine hands to wander mortal realms.', 'From fuzzy to ferocious in an instant.', 'Get carried away.', 'Gnolls make offerings to sinister forces in the shadow-drenched chasms.', 'Gruul territorial markings need not be legible. The blood, snot, and muck used to smear them are unmistakably Gruul.', 'Hatred outlives the hateful.', 'He collects the precious metals, and then converts the rest to propellant.', 'Idle chatter beckons many an attentive ear.', "If it can't be had here, it can't be had on any world.", 'If you stop to listen, you can hear it grow.', 'In the autumn, she casts her seeds across the streets below, and come spring, her children rise in service to the Conclave.', 'It fears no sword and leaves no bones behind.', 'It shambled from the cloud of ash and bone dust, undeterred by its own extinction.', 'It started as a mere drop of water. The Magic Mirror crystallized it into much more.', 'Its beak rends flesh and bone, exposing the tender marrow of dream.', 'Its collapse is like the lashing out of a long-dead civilization that resents being forgotten.', 'Its wings shimmer with dreams absorbed from its enemies.', 'Late at night, when dreams touch a studious mind, bouts of inspiration strike.', 'Legend says a mighty angel appears to pilgrims in need who reach this lofty height.', 'Liliana whispered to whatever consciousness Oketra and Bontu had left. "You are the gods. He is the usurper. You know what to do."', "Lost to time is the artificer's art of trapping light from a distant star in a ring of purest gold.", 'Made of bone and boiled in blood, a Rakdos signet is not considered finished until it has been used as a murder weapon.', 'Many necromancers share the same last words—the ones that conclude the undeath ritual.', "Merfolk don't always know what they're looking for, but they're certain once they find it.", "Mirrodin's creator still lives, still shapes metal, and still commands world-shaking power.", 'Much more painful than mere regret.', 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', 'No one is as dedicated to perfection as a stitcher working on their latest masterpiece.', 'No one returns unchanged.', 'No thought is as succulent as a secret.', 'Not alive, not dead, but definitely furious.', 'On the continent of Tazeem, rushing waters plunge through narrow canyons into mist-cloaked lakes.', 'On the volcanic continent of Akoum, bizarre vegetation clusters around gas vents, and jagged mountain peaks rise high into the air.', 'One offering to appease her on her arrival. Another to celebrate her departure.', 'One who wears magical *boots of striding and springing* can jump astounding distances.', 'Only one vault was great enough to hold Emrakul.', 'Out of sight, into mind.', 'Plant life in the valley changes for the worse as runoff from dwarven forges contaminates the water.', 'Ride into legend.', "Serum was once derived from Mirrodin's blinkmoths, offering visions of inspiration. Now it is pulled from Phyrexian inkmoths, yielding visions of perfection.", 'She follows the old tributaries built when merrows still shaped the tides.', 'Take two steps north into the unsettled future, south into the unquiet past, east into the present day, or west into the great unknown.', 'The aberrant magic of the Rimewind drew the unicorns back from the northern wastes to do battle once again.', 'The ancient magic of sun elves keeps these lands in an eternal summer.', "The blade glows only for Zendikar's chosen.", 'The continent of Guul Draz is a geothermal swampland reeking of heat and decay.', 'The continent of Murasa lies beneath a blanket of dense vegetation, its enormous branches tangled so thickly that some inhabitants never see the ground.', 'The continent of Ondu is a vast plateau crisscrossed by deep trenches and meandering rivers.', 'The enormous can still be at the mercy of the small.', 'The forge of Purphoros burns in the heart of Mount Velus, attracting dragons with its blistering heat.', 'The impact sent the soldiers scattering—then something came out of the crater.', 'The mizzium-sphere array drove her mind deep into the thought field, where only the rarest motes of genius may be plucked.', 'The mountain will build your cairn of snow and ice and stone.', 'The power of a waterfall. The fury of an avalanche. The intellect of a gale-force wind.', 'The smallest seed of regret can bloom into redemption.', 'The storm rages and the earth breaks.', 'The true strength of nature is not the raging storm or the charging rhino, but the inexorable vitality of life.', 'The wilds consume, but they also create.', 'There may exist powers even greater than Phyrexia.', 'Those who worship the great gargantuans could hardly be expected to fight with a subtle weapon.', 'Those with knowledge are wise to listen to those with imagination.', 'Though Volrath is long dead, the slivers have become everything he wanted them to be: mindless instruments of destruction and despair.', "To consult a sphinx is a test in patience. Perhaps that's the point.", "To find its center is to find one's own.", 'Underdark flooding has swallowed ancient drow burial chambers, which are now haunted . . . and infested with oozes.', 'What was supposed to be a quiet time in town turned into an adventure of its own.', "When killing five just isn't enough.", 'Which burns more fiercely? Your ambition, or the flame?', 'Wildflowers here bloom not with the season but with the ebb and flow of magic.']
artist: ['Aaron J. Riley', 'Adam Paquette', 'Adam Rex', 'Alayna Danner', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Alex Konstad', 'Alexander Mokhov', 'Allen Williams', 'Andrew Mar', 'Andrey Kuzinskiy', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Antonio José Manzanedo', 'Austin Hsu', 'Billy Christian', 'Brian Hagan', 'Brian Valeza', 'Bryan Sola', 'Caio Monteiro', 'Campbell White', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Carmen Sinek', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Ostrowski', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Chris Seaman', 'Christine Choi', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Rapoza', 'Denman Rooke', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Dmitry Burmak', 'Dominick Domingo', 'Donato Giancola', 'Drew Baker', 'Drew Tucker', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eric Fortune', 'Evan Shipard', 'Even Amundsen', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Gabor Szikszai', 'Glen Angus', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Heather Hudson', 'Heonhwa Choe', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Irina Nordsol', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jake Murray', 'Jakub Kasper', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jarel Threat', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Joe Slucher', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Jonathan Kuo', 'Josu Hernaiz', 'Jung Park', 'Justin Sweet', 'Justyna Dura', 'Kamila Szutenberg', 'Kari Christensen', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Kim Sokol', 'Kimonas Theodossiou', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lie Setiawan', 'Lindsey Look', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Manuel Castañón', 'Mark Winters', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Milivoj Ćeran', 'Min Yum', 'Nicholas Gregory', 'Nils Hamm', 'Olena Richards', 'Olivier Bernard', 'PINDURSKI', 'Pat Lewis', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Randy Vargas', 'Ravenna Tran', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebekah Lynn', 'Ron Spears', 'Rudy Siswanto', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Sam White', 'Sam Wolfe Connelly', 'Scott Chou', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Sean Murray', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Sidharth Chaturvedi', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Stephen Tappin', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Titus Lunter', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomas Duchek', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Tristan Elwell', 'Ulrich Brunin', 'Uriah Voth', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Viko Menezes', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'William Wu', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Wisnu Tan', 'YW Tang', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yongjae Choi', 'Zoltan Boros']
